<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, English-first. The opponent denies determinate judgments; the reply draws the consequence that Buddhist and non-Buddhist systems and teachers could not be ranked. 'Given the statements that have come above' and 'one way or the other' are complete contextual recasts at d3; chos thams cad → anything is a noun phrase, not a dictionary word. Both grub mtha' occurrences own the two 'system' occurrences. The two phyi rol pa occurrences retain 'non-Buddhist' and the original 'non- Buddhists'. sangs rgyas pa → Buddha follows this row's institutional paraphrase, not a general equivalence between Buddhist and Buddha. bdag cag licenses 'our'. bzang ngan is omitted because its comparison is distributed across 'all the same' and 'difference in their correctness'; no false null is used. Terminal med owns the explicit 'no' once; its scope also informs the recast 'never state'. thal owns the first 'must be suggesting that' once, while the second implication is supplied repetition. sogs and zhes zer na are omitted because their discourse contributions have no securely isolated atom. All supplied participants, articles and auxiliary framing stay unwrapped.</div>
